.TH ___CYAML_DESTROY 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
___cyaml_destroy \- RAII cleanup wrapper for cyaml handles
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cyaml.h>

void ___cyaml_destroy(cyaml *node);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Called automatically by the GCC cleanup attribute when a scoped cyaml
variable goes out of scope (registered by cyaml_declare_scoped()).
Frees *node with __cyaml_destroy() and sets *node to NULL.  Safe to
call when *node is already NULL.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cyaml_declare_scoped (macro) (3),
.BR __cyaml_destroy (3)
